Adam and Bonnie are sitting in a restaurant; Mary is sitting a few tables away. 
A: Why does Mary have her purse on her lap?  (not BEL? QUD)
A: Where does Mary think her wallet is? (BEL? QUD)
B: If her purse is hanging on her chair, she doesn’t know that her wallet is missing.
How likely is it that Mary’s wallet is missing?

Is the speaker asking whether Mary believes that her wallet was stolen? (question about BEL)
Is the speaker asking whether the wallet was stolen (question about CC; no)
Does Mary know that her wallet was stolen? 
Does Mary know that her wallet was stolen, if her purse hangs on her chair? 

A: Why does Mary have her purse on her lap?  (not POST? QUD)
A: Is Mary worrying about her wallet? (POST? QUD)
B: If her purse is hanging on her chair, she doesn’t stop worrying about her wallet when the food arrives.
How likely is it that Mary worries about her wallet before the food arrives?




If John covered his tracks, then Mary doesn’t know that he’s cheating on her.

If I use this phrase later, then they know that I’m in trouble.
If John uses this phrase later, then his enemies know that he’s in trouble.

Some doctors believe that this type of radiation is a cure, others don’t. What kind of doctor is Dr. Michael? What does he believe? (not a good QUD for the sentence, despite BEL? usually being a good QUD)

If the PSA rises, then Dr. Michael doesn’t know that this type of radiation is a cure. (no projection)
If the PSA rises, then Dr. Michael doesn’t stop suggesting this type of radiation. (projection)

QUD is more likely about notPOST in conditionals than about BEL, so we get projection of PRE but not of CC.